{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat results/ideas/02_cross_fitted_tail_adaptive_residual_scaling/program_1/src/METHOD.md; sed -n '1,240p' results/ideas/02_cross_fitted_tail_adaptive_residual_scaling/program_1/src/program.py; jq '.final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence | {keys:keys,episode_count,status,episode0:(.episodes[0]|{seed,score,solution_keys:(.solution|keys),cases:[.solution.cases[]|{case,variants:(.variants|keys)}],paired_seed_intervals:.solution.paired_seed_intervals})}' paper_data.json; rg --files -L task | head -50; cat results/conclusions.md; cat results/best_program_manifest.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat results/ideas/02_cross_fitted_tail_adaptive_residual_scaling/program_1/src/METHOD.md; sed -n '1,240p' results/ideas/02_cross_fitted_tail_adaptive_residual_scaling/program_1/src/program.py; jq '.final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence | {keys:keys,episode_count,status,episode0:(.episodes[0]|{seed,score,solution_keys:(.solution|keys),cases:[.solution.cases[]|{case,variants:(.variants|keys)}],paired_seed_intervals:.solution.paired_seed_intervals})}' paper_data.json; rg --files -L task | head -50; cat results/conclusions.md; cat results/best_program_manifest.json\"","aggregated_output":"# Cross-fitted tail-adaptive residual scaling\n\n## Scope and interface\n\n`program.py:handle` retains the starter's fit/predict/reset and bounded-transfer\nprotocol. Only supplied training covariates and training residual norms enter\nlearning. Fit still returns only `{\"ok\": true}`; predict still returns only the\nencoded float64 `scales` array. Calibration, composition centers, geometry, and\nregion construction remain evaluator-owned. No extra observations are assumed.\n\n## Prespecified learner\n\n- The incumbent remains quadratic-feature ridge regression of log residual norm,\n  with fold-local centering, standardization, the original ridge penalties, and\n  original log-prediction bounds. Its original residual floor is retained.\n- The tail learner targets the 0.9 quantile of\n  `log(max(residual_norm, 1e-12))`. This is a surrogate learning target, not an\n  assumed conformal miscoverage level.\n- Each stump uses training-only thresholds at 15 equally spaced quantile levels\n  from 0.05 to 0.95 for each supplied feature. Both leaves require at least\n  `max(20, ceil(0.03 * fitting_sample_size))` observations. Updates are within-leaf\n  empirical residual quantiles. The learning rate is 0.1; at most 80 rounds are\n  fitted, stopping when no candidate reduces training pinball loss beyond a\n  numerical tolerance. Constant features and undersized folds yield an\n  intercept-only tail predictor. Repeated residual values are allowed.\n- To avoid repeatedly sorting every leaf, each round sorts working residuals\n  once. Cumulative membership counts recover interpolated leaf quantiles; exact\n  pinball losses of the shrunken updates choose the split. The selected leaf\n  updates are then recomputed with NumPy's empirical quantile operation.\n- Three deterministic folds use `np.random.default_rng(0).permutation(n)` and\n  `np.array_split`. Each fold fits its own incumbent preprocessing, tail\n  thresholds, and quantile alignment offsets using only fitting observations.\n- Six candidates, in fixed simplicity order, are incumbent, constant, and\n  log-space incumbent/tail blends with tail weights 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, and 1.0.\n  Every candidate receives a fitting-only additive log offset equal to the\n  empirical 0.9 quantile of target minus fitted log scale. Aligning a blend this\n  way is unchanged by first applying constant offsets to its component models.\n- Candidate losses are mean validation pinball losses within each fold. Their\n  unweighted fold means are compared; the standard error is the sample standard\n  deviation across the three fold losses divided by sqrt(3). The first candidate\n  within one standard error of the lowest mean loss is selected. This is a\n  regularization heuristic, not a significance test or a confidence interval:\n  fitting folds overlap. For fewer than three training observations the\n  incumbent is used without cross-validation. Empty training arrays are rejected.\n- Models and offsets are refitted using all training observations. Prediction is\n  read-only and does not depend on query-batch statistics. Selected log scales\n  are bounded to [-30, 30] before exponentiation, with a positive numerical floor.\n  The documented evaluator additionally clips scales to [0.0001, 10000].\n\nNo aggregate evaluation feedback enters any choice. Reset seeds retain their\nprotocol meaning and do not select workloads or hyperparameters. Selection\nstatistics are internal and are not added to RPC responses.\n\n## Validity argument and limitations\n\nCondition on the training data and all fitting choices. The learned scale is\nthen a fixed strictly positive function. If calibration and test observations\nare exchangeable conditional on those choices, and use the same evaluator-owned\ncenter, geometry, and numerical scale clipping, their normalized residual scores\nare exchangeable. For m calibration scores and k = ceil((m+1)(1-alpha)), the usual\nsplit-conformal threshold at rank k (infinity if k > m) gives marginal coverage\nat least 1-alpha, with ties conservative. Training-only selection does not change\nthis rank argument. It does not imply conditional/group coverage, nor validity\nunder distribution shift or calibration reuse. The argument presumes the\nevaluator actually uses this split-conformal construction; the candidate does\nnot inspect or alter it.\n\nPinball loss on log norms is not simplex volume or the harness objective. The\nselection rule may favor an inferior efficiency tradeoff. Additive stumps miss\ninteractions; irrelevant features, small samples, finite threshold grids, and\ntail sparsity can impair learning. Numerical clipping can limit adaptivity and\nbreak otherwise irrelevant global-scale invariance. No improvement, runtime,\ncoverage, or uncertainty estimate for the harness metrics has been measured.\n\n## Execution status\n\nThis stage permits source edits and static filesystem checks only. No candidate,\ntests, benchmark, evaluator, package manager, network request, or exploratory\ncomputation was executed. Positivity, batch-invariance, degeneracy, and protocol\ntests remain unperformed; their expected behavior is supported only by source\nreasoning, not test evidence. The official evaluation is harness-owned.\n\nThis is a candidate implementation, not a completed research paper. Repeated-run\nexperiments, numerical uncertainty quantification, literature review, an official\nconference-template manuscript/PDF and checklist, measured dependency versions,\nand measured resource use remain incomplete. No fabricated results, citations,\nor paper claims are supplied. No prohibited literature was accessed.\n\"\"\"Train-only positive compositional residual-scale learner, python_rpc_v1:handle.\n\nAll requests/responses are finite JSON objects; extra response keys are forbidden.\nreset: {op:'reset', seed: nonnegative int} -> {ok:true}. Clears all model/transfer\nstate. Any seed is accepted; seeds initialize randomness, never select a workload.\nfit: {op:'fit', x:Array[n,6], residuals:Array[n], dimension:int>=2,\n      scale_min:0.0001, scale_max:10000.0} -> {ok:true}.\nOnly training covariates and training residual norms are provided. Fits replace the\nmodel. Prediction is read-only and requires a completed fit after reset.\npredict: {op:'predict', x:Array[n,6]} -> {scales:Array[n]}.\nReturn strictly positive finite scales; the evaluator consistently clips them to\n[0.0001,10000]. No calibration/test outcomes or later scoring feedback is given.\nArray is exactly {encoding:'base64',dtype:'<f8',shape:[...],nbytes:int,data:str}.\nData is C-order little-endian float64, n<=2048 normally; no file paths are used.\nWorkload dimensions/settings come from fit, not reset seeds. Candidate changes may\nchange the scale estimator but not evaluator-owned center, geometry or calibration.\n\nOptional bounded fallback, exercised by maximum-protocol tests, not needed for\nordinary shapes: begin {op:'begin',method:'fit'|'predict',fields:object,\narrays:{name:{shape:list,nbytes:int}},nbytes:int} -> {token:str}.\nfields holds the non-array logical request fields except op. Arrays, in insertion\norder, concatenate raw <f8 bytes; total <=8 MiB. upload {op:'upload',token:str,\noffset:int,data:base64str} -> {ok:true}, sequential <=2 chunks of <=4 MiB.\ncommit {op:'commit',token:str} -> {ok:true} validates lengths and computes once.\nexport_start {op:'export_start',token:str} -> {nbytes:int,chunks:int}.\nfetch {op:'fetch',token:str,index:int} -> {data:base64str}, sequential <=2 chunks.\nOutput is UTF-8 JSON for fit, raw <f8 scales for predict. release\n{op:'release',token:str} -> {ok:true} destroys buffers. One live token, <=32 MiB\ntransfer storage; reset invalidates it. No token is a path. At most 8 calls per\nlogical operation (begin,2 uploads,commit,export_start,2 fetches,release).\nNo self-reported learning, timing or diagnostics are accepted as scientific evidence.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport json\nimport math\nimport numpy as np\n\nMODEL = None\nTRANSFER = None\nCHUNK = 4 * 1024 * 1024\n\n\ndef decode(value):\n    if set(value) != {'encoding', 'dtype', 'shape', 'nbytes', 'data'}:\n        raise ValueError('array schema')\n    if value['encoding'] != 'base64' or value['dtype'] != '<f8':\n        raise ValueError('array encoding')\n    raw = base64.b64decode(value['data'], validate=True)\n    if len(raw) != value['nbytes'] or len(raw) != math.prod(value['shape']) * 8:\n        raise ValueError('array size')\n    result = np.frombuffer(raw, dtype='<f8').reshape(value['shape'])\n    if not np.isfinite(result).all():\n        raise ValueError('nonfinite input')\n    return result\n\n\ndef encode(array):\n    array = np.asarray(array, dtype='<f8', order='C')\n    return dict(encoding='base64', dtype='<f8', shape=list(array.shape),\n                nbytes=array.nbytes, data=base64.b64encode(array.tobytes()).decode('ascii'))\n\n\ndef features(array):\n    return np.column_stack((np.ones(len(array)), array, array * array))\n\n\ndef pinball_loss(target, prediction, quantile):\n    return np.maximum(quantile * (target - prediction), (quantile - 1.0) * (target - prediction))\n\n\ndef blend_log_scales(incumbent_log_scale, tail_log_scale, tail_weight):\n    return (1.0 - tail_weight) * incumbent_log_scale + tail_weight * tail_log_scale\n\n\ndef quantiles_from_counts(sorted_values, cumulative_counts, leaf_sizes, quantile):\n    positions = quantile * (leaf_sizes - 1)\n    lower_ranks = np.floor(positions)\n    upper_ranks = np.ceil(positions)\n    lower_indices = np.argmax(cumulative_counts > lower_ranks[:, None], axis=1)\n    upper_indices = np.argmax(cumulative_counts > upper_ranks[:, None], axis=1)\n    return (sorted_values[lower_indices]\n            + (positions - lower_ranks)\n            * (sorted_values[upper_indices] - sorted_values[lower_indices]))\n\n\ndef fit_quantile_stumps(features, log_norms, quantile, max_rounds, min_leaf):\n    learning_rate = 0.1\n    intercept = float(np.quantile(log_norms, quantile))\n    model = dict(intercept=intercept, learning_rate=learning_rate, stumps=[])\n    fitted_log_scale = np.full(len(log_norms), intercept)\n    if len(log_norms) < 2 * min_leaf:\n        return model\n    splits, masks = [], []\n    for feature_index in range(features.shape[1]):\n        thresholds = np.unique(np.quantile(features[:, feature_index],\n                                           np.linspace(0.05, 0.95, 15)))\n        for threshold in thresholds:\n            left_mask = features[:, feature_index] <= threshold\n            left_size = int(left_mask.sum())\n            if min_leaf <= left_size <= len(log_norms) - min_leaf:\n                splits.append((feature_index, float(threshold)))\n                masks.append(left_mask)\n    if not splits:\n        return model\n    split_masks = np.asarray(masks, dtype=bool)\n    left_sizes = split_masks.sum(axis=1)\n    right_sizes = len(log_norms) - left_sizes\n    observation_counts = np.arange(1, len(log_norms) + 1)\n    for round_index in range(min(max_rounds, 80)):\n        working_residuals = log_norms - fitted_log_scale\n        sorted_indices = np.argsort(working_residuals, kind='stable')\n        sorted_values = working_residuals[sorted_indices]\n        left_counts = np.cumsum(split_masks[:, sorted_indices], axis=1)\n        left_updates = quantiles_from_counts(sorted_values, left_counts,\n                                            left_sizes, quantile)\n        right_updates = quantiles_from_counts(sorted_values,\n                                             observation_counts - left_counts,\n                                             right_sizes, quantile)\n        updates = learning_rate * np.where(split_masks, left_updates[:, None],\n                                          right_updates[:, None])\n        losses = pinball_loss(working_residuals[None, :], updates, quantile).mean(axis=1)\n        best_index = int(np.argmin(losses))\n        current_loss = float(pinball_loss(working_residuals, 0.0, quantile).mean())\n        if losses[best_index] >= current_loss - 1e-12 * max(1.0, current_loss):\n            break\n        left_mask = split_masks[best_index]\n        left_update = float(np.quantile(working_residuals[left_mask], quantile))\n        right_update = float(np.quantile(working_residuals[~left_mask], quantile))\n        fitted_log_scale += learning_rate * np.where(left_mask, left_update, right_update)\n        feature_index, threshold = splits[best_index]\n        model['stumps'].append((feature_index, threshold, left_update, right_update))\n    return model\n\n\ndef predict_quantile_stumps(model, covariates):\n    prediction = np.full(len(covariates), model['intercept'])\n    for feature_index, threshold, left_update, right_update in model['stumps']:\n        left_mask = covariates[:, feature_index] <= threshold\n        prediction += model['learning_rate'] * np.where(left_mask, left_update, right_update)\n    return prediction\n\n\ndef fit_incumbent(covariates, residual_norms):\n    mean = covariates.mean(axis=0)\n    deviation = np.maximum(covariates.std(axis=0), 1e-8)\n    design = features((covariates - mean) / deviation)\n    target = np.log(np.maximum(residual_norms, 1e-8))\n    penalty = np.eye(design.shape[1]) * 2.0\n    penalty[0, 0] = 1e-8\n    coefficients = np.linalg.solve(design.T @ design + penalty, design.T @ target)\n    return mean, deviation, coefficients\n\n\ndef predict_incumbent_log(model, covariates):\n    mean, deviation, coefficients = model\n    return np.clip(features((covariates - mean) / deviation) @ coefficients,\n                   np.log(1e-4), np.log(1e4))\n\n\ndef raw_candidate_logs(incumbent, tail_model, covariates):\n    incumbent_log_scale = predict_incumbent_log(incumbent, covariates)\n    tail_log_scale = predict_quantile_stumps(tail_model, covariates)\n    return np.column_stack((incumbent_log_scale, np.zeros(len(covariates)),\n                            *(blend_log_scales(incumbent_log_scale, tail_log_scale, weight)\n                              for weight in (0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0))))\n\n\ndef align_log_scale(log_norms, fitted_log_scale, quantile):\n    alignment_offset = float(np.quantile(log_norms - fitted_log_scale, quantile))\n    return alignment_offset\n\n\ndef fit_scale_family(covariates, residual_norms, log_norms, tail_model, quantile):\n    incumbent = fit_incumbent(covariates, residual_norms)\n    fitted_candidates = raw_candidate_logs(incumbent, tail_model, covariates)\n    offsets = np.asarray([align_log_scale(log_norms, fitted_candidates[:, index], quantile)\n                          for index in range(fitted_candidates.shape[1])])\n    return dict(incumbent=incumbent, tail=tail_model, alignment_offsets=offsets)\n\n\ndef fit_scale(features, residual_norms):\n    quantile, max_rounds = 0.9, 80\n    log_norms = np.log(np.maximum(residual_norms, 1e-12))\n    selected_index = 0\n    if len(log_norms) >= 3:\n        indices = np.random.default_rng(0).permutation(len(log_norms))\n        folds = np.array_split(indices, 3)\n        fold_losses = []\n        for fold_index, validation_indices in enumerate(folds):\n            fit_indices = np.concatenate([fold for index, fold in enumerate(folds)\n                                          if index != fold_index])\n            assert np.intersect1d(fit_indices, validation_indices).size == 0\n            min_leaf = max(20, math.ceil(0.03 * len(fit_indices)))\n            fold_tail_model = fit_quantile_stumps(features[fit_indices], log_norms[fit_indices], quantile, max_rounds, min_leaf)\n            family = fit_scale_family(features[fit_indices], residual_norms[fit_indices],\n                                      log_norms[fit_indices], fold_tail_model, quantile)\n            held_out = raw_candidate_logs(family['incumbent'], family['tail'],\n                                          features[validation_indices])\n            held_out += family['alignment_offsets']\n            fold_losses.append(pinball_loss(log_norms[validation_indices, None],\n                                            held_out, quantile).mean(axis=0))\n        fold_losses = np.asarray(fold_losses)\n        mean_losses = fold_losses.mean(axis=0)\n        standard_errors = fold_losses.std(axis=0, ddof=1) / np.sqrt(len(folds))\n        best_index = int(np.argmin(mean_losses))\n        selection_limit = mean_losses[best_index] + standard_errors[best_index]\n        simplicity_order = (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5)\n        selected_index = next(index for index in simplicity_order if mean_losses[index] <= selection_limit)\n    min_leaf = max(20, math.ceil(0.03 * len(log_norms)))\n    tail_model = fit_quantile_stumps(features, log_norms, quantile, max_rounds, min_leaf)\n    model = fit_scale_family(features, residual_norms, log_norms, tail_model, quantile)\n    model['selected_index'] = selected_index\n    return model\n\n\ndef predict_scale(model, covariates):\n    selected_index = model['selected_index']\n    if selected_index == 1:\n        raw_log_scale = np.zeros(len(covariates))\n    elif selected_index == 0:\n        raw_log_scale = predict_incumbent_log(model['incumbent'], covariates)\n    else:\n        incumbent_log_scale = predict_incumbent_log(model['incumbent'], covariates)\n        tail_log_scale = predict_quantile_stumps(model['tail'], covariates)\n        tail_weight = (0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0)[selected_index - 2]\n        raw_log_scale = blend_log_scales(incumbent_log_scale, tail_log_scale, tail_weight)\n    alignment_offset = model['alignment_offsets'][selected_index]\n    blended_log_scale = raw_log_scale + alignment_offset\n    return np.maximum(np.exp(np.clip(blended_log_scale, -30.0, 30.0)), 1e-12)\n\n\ndef compute(method, fields, arrays):\n    global MODEL\n    if method == 'fit':\n        covariates, residuals = arrays['x'], arrays['residuals']\n        if covariates.ndim != 2 or covariates.shape[1] != 6 or residuals.shape != (len(covariates),):\n            raise ValueError('training shape')\n        if len(covariates) == 0:\n            raise ValueError('empty training data')\n        MODEL = fit_scale(covariates, residuals)\n{\n  \"keys\": [\n    \"candidate_diagnostics_trust\",\n    \"episode_count\",\n    \"episodes\",\n    \"path\",\n    \"sha256\",\n    \"status\"\n  ],\n  \"episode_count\": 6,\n  \"status\": \"available\",\n  \"episode0\": {\n    \"seed\": 1009,\n    \"score\": 0.8769290665561597,\n    \"solution_keys\": [\n      \"cases\",\n      \"manifest_sha256\",\n      \"paired_seed_intervals\",\n      \"productive_baseline_seconds\",\n      \"serialized_payload_preflight\"\n    ],\n    \"cases\": [\n      {\n        \"case\": \"H3\",\n        \"variants\": [\n          \"actual\",\n          \"constant\",\n          \"permuted\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"case\": \"H10\",\n        \"variants\": [\n          \"actual\",\n          \"constant\",\n          \"permuted\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"case\": \"B3\",\n        \"variants\": [\n          \"actual\",\n          \"constant\",\n          \"permuted\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"case\": \"B10\",\n        \"variants\": [\n          \"actual\",\n          \"constant\",\n          \"permuted\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"case\": \"S3\",\n        \"variants\": [\n          \"actual\",\n          \"constant\",\n          \"permuted\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"case\": \"S10\",\n        \"variants\": [\n          \"actual\",\n          \"constant\",\n          \"permuted\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"paired_seed_intervals\": {\n      \"bonferroni\": [\n        0.026003782978225698,\n        0.031205719394701972\n      ],\n      \"constant\": [\n        0.043901240346666696,\n        0.050616967867983816\n      ],\n      \"global_ilr\": [\n        0.043901240346666696,\n        0.050616967867983816\n      ],\n      \"permuted\": [\n        0.0431322485143756,\n        0.05108793994305608\n      ],\n      \"raw_linf\": [\n        0.028311622704360995,\n        0.032678904974567095\n      ],\n      \"uncalibrated\": [\n        0.04434467186215206,\n        0.04862424919069211\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\ntask/task.md\ntask/task_contract.json\ntask/evaluate_final.py\ntask/evaluate.py\ntask/resources/search/production-B3-211.json\ntask/resources/search/smoke-H3-101.json\ntask/resources/search/production-B10-307.json\ntask/resources/search/production-S3-211.json\ntask/resources/search/production-S10-101.json\ntask/resources/search/smoke-H10-101.json\ntask/resources/search/smoke-S3-101.json\ntask/resources/search/production-H3-101.json\ntask/resources/search/production-B10-101.json\ntask/resources/search/production-S10-211.json\ntask/resources/search/smoke-B10-101.json\ntask/resources/search/smoke-S10-101.json\ntask/resources/search/production-S3-307.json\ntask/resources/search/production-H3-211.json\ntask/resources/search/production-H3-307.json\ntask/resources/search/production-H10-307.json\ntask/resources/search/production-B10-211.json\ntask/resources/search/production-S10-307.json\ntask/resources/search/production-S3-101.json\ntask/resources/search/manifest.json\ntask/resources/search/production-B3-307.json\ntask/resources/search/production-B3-101.json\ntask/resources/search/smoke-B3-101.json\ntask/res